      "source": [
        "# Session 1: Database Introduction & SQL Basics\n",
        "\n",
        "This interactive notebook covers foundational concepts of Relational Database Management Systems (RDBMS), SQL DDL/DML, and hands-on query operations for **Session 1: Database Introduction & SQL Basics**.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Overview of Tasks\n",
        "- **Task 1:** Install & verify MySQL / SQLite database connectivity (`music_streaming_app`).\n",
        "- **Task 2:** Create `playlists` table with columns (`playlist_id`, `name`, `created_by`).\n",
        "- **Task 3:** Insert three sample rows representing playlists like 'Bollywood Hits', 'Chill Vibes', and 'Workout Mix'.\n",
        "- **Task 4:** Write an SQL SELECT query to filter playlists created by 'Amit' using the `WHERE` clause.\n",
        "- **Task 5:** Conceptual explanation: Difference between a Table, a Row, and a Column using a Zomato food delivery example."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Task 1: Database Setup & Connectivity\n",
        "Initialize connection to our database engine."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import sqlite3\n",
        "import os\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "os.makedirs(\"database\", exist_ok=True)\n",
        "db_path = os.path.join(\"database\", \"music_streaming_app.db\")\n",
        "conn = sqlite3.connect(db_path)\n",
        "cursor = conn.cursor()\n",
        "print(f\"Connected to SQLite {sqlite3.sqlite_version} at: {db_path}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Task 2: Create 'playlists' Table\n",
        "Define table structure inside `music_streaming_app`:\n",
        "- `playlist_id`: Integer, Primary Key, Auto-increment\n",
        "- `name`: Varchar(100), Playlist title\n",
        "- `created_by`: Varchar(50), Username of the playlist creator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "cursor.execute(\"DROP TABLE IF EXISTS playlists;\")\n",
        "\n",
        "create_table_sql = \"\"\"\n",
        "CREATE TABLE playlists (\n",
        "    playlist_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n",
        "    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,\n",
        "    created_by VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,\n",
        "    created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n",
        ");\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "cursor.execute(create_table_sql)\n",
        "conn.commit()\n",
        "print(\"Table 'playlists' created successfully!\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Task 3: Insert Sample Rows\n",
        "Insert sample playlists created by different users ('Amit', 'Priya', 'Rohan')."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "sample_playlists = [\n",
        "    (\"Bollywood Hits\", \"Amit\"),\n",
        "    (\"Chill Vibes\", \"Priya\"),\n",
        "    (\"Workout Mix\", \"Rohan\"),\n",
        "    (\"Retro 90s Classics\", \"Amit\")\n",
        "]\n",
        "\n",
        "cursor.executemany(\n",
        "    \"INSERT INTO playlists (name, created_by) VALUES (?, ?);\",\n",
        "    sample_playlists\n",
        ")\n",
        "conn.commit()\n",
        "print(f\"Successfully inserted {len(sample_playlists)} records.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Task 4: Filter by User 'Amit' Using WHERE Clause\n",
        "Retrieve only playlists where `created_by = 'Amit'`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "query = \"\"\"\n",
        "SELECT playlist_id, name, created_by, created_at\n",
        "FROM playlists\n",
        "WHERE created_by = 'Amit';\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "\n",
        "df_amit = pd.read_sql_query(query, conn)\n",
        "print(\"Playlists created by Amit:\")\n",
        "display(df_amit)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Task 5: Conceptual Explanation - Table vs Row vs Column\n",
        "\n",
        "Using a food delivery app like **Zomato**:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Component | Definition | Zomato Real-World Analogy |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| **Table** | The complete 2D dataset representing an entire entity collection. | The entire `restaurants` database table holding every restaurant on Zomato across all cities. |\n",
        "| **Column** | A vertical slice defining a specific attribute or field across all records. | `cuisine`, `rating`, `location`. Every restaurant must have a rating (e.g. 4.5). |\n",
        "| **Row** | A single horizontal record representing one unique, individual instance. | One specific restaurant card in the app: `[ID: 101, Name: 'Haldiram\'s', Rating: 4.3, Location: 'Delhi']`. |"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# Display complete table for verification\n",
        "df_all = pd.read_sql_query(\"SELECT * FROM playlists;\", conn)\n",
        "print(\"Complete Playlists Table:\")\n",
        "display(df_all)\n",
        "\n",
        "conn.close()"
      ]
    }
  ],
